=== PARITY (vs web DriveHighlightSlide.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> useTranslation + useUnits ONLY. The web leaf is presentational: its
    parent (SlideRenderer) passes `drive`, a localized `label`, and an `emoji`. The native
    surface mirrors this — the P1/S8 DriveHighlightSource carries that prop snapshot + the
    distance preference + load/freshness status; the view performs NO HTTP.
  Conversion -> distance: convertDistanceFromSI(distance_km*1000, unit) [km/mi/ft divisors
    1000 / 1609.344 / 0.3048]; efficiency: unit==='mi' ? wh_km*1.609344 : wh_km, with the
    'Wh/mi' vs 'Wh/km' suffix; both rounded with Math.round parity (half away from zero,
    no grouping). Duration: floor(min/60)+'h '+min%60+'m' or just 'm'. Reproduced VERBATIM
    and PROVEN by host execution (below): 412.7 km->413, 178.4 Wh/km->178, 312 min->"5h 12m";
    23.5 km->15 mi, 132 Wh/km->212 Wh/mi.
  States -> every state renders: loading (skeleton), empty (web !drive: emoji + "No drive
    data for this year"), error (QueryError-equivalent + retry), stale/offline (freshness
    chip over the cached recap), content (animated card). No hidden surfaces.
  Motion -> web @/components/motion mapped to native: label/card via shared TSFadeIn
    (Reduce-Motion aware); the emoji's spring (scale 0->1, rotate -10->0, stiffness 180,
    damping 14) via SwiftUI interpolatingSpring(stiffness:180, damping:14), static under
    Reduce Motion.
  i18n -> all strings via the P1/S10 facade; the two web keys (yearReview.noDriveData,
    yearReview.duration) carry their exact en.json values; recap label/emoji are parent-
    supplied (not owned here). No hardcoded English literals in the view.
  a11y -> populated slide is one combined VoiceOver element (label, route, distance,
    duration, efficiency, date); decorative glyphs accessibilityHidden; retry has a label;
    Dynamic Type via tokens; Reduce Motion honored.

